<h1>Delete account & data</h1>
<p class="lead">Learn how to delete your JobStamp account and associated personal account data.</p>

<section><h2>Delete your account directly in JobStamp</h2>
<p>If you still have access to the app, you can initiate deletion directly in JobStamp.</p>
<div class="box"><ol><li>Open JobStamp.</li><li>Open Settings.</li><li>Go to your user account section.</li><li>Select <strong>“Delete account”</strong>.</li><li>Confirm the deletion as described in the app.</li></ol></div>
</section>
<section><h2>Request deletion without access to the app</h2>
<p>If you no longer have access to JobStamp, you can request account deletion by email.</p>
<div class="box important"><p><strong><a href="mailto:pabaapps@web.de?subject=JobStamp%20-%20Account%20deletion">pabaapps@web.de</a></strong></p><p>If possible, use the email address registered with your JobStamp account so we can identify the account.</p></div>
</section>
<section><h2>What is removed?</h2>
<ul><li>the JobStamp sign-in account,</li><li>personal account links and company memberships,</li><li>the link between the account and an employee profile,</li><li>personal profile data where no longer required,</li><li>personally assigned feedback and active personal timer data.</li></ul>
<p>Business records may be anonymised or detached from the deleted user identifier where they must be retained for legal or operational documentation purposes.</p>
</section>
<section><h2>Special case for company owners</h2>
<p>If the account is the last owner of a company, ownership must first be transferred to another linked user account or the company and its associated company data must be permanently deleted.</p>
</section>
<section><h2>Retention obligations</h2>
<p>Where legal obligations or other lawful grounds require certain data to be retained, the data will only be processed for the required retention period and deleted afterwards.</p>
</section>

